CORE
JmlTernary
--function JmlTernary.clampLow10 --jml-source src/main/java/JmlTernary.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for JML ternary expressions in postconditions.

Pre-fix: jml_lowering.cpp's type-propagation pass handled
arithmetic, relational and logical operators but NOT if_exprt
(C-style ternary). When the parser built `cond ? a : b` with
empty type (operands not yet resolved), the empty type would
flow into downstream construction, causing solver type
mismatches.

Post-fix: if_exprt has its type set to operand[1]'s type
(the then-branch) after operand recursion. The else-branch
type must match (Java semantics) and is checked downstream.
